# Subsurface and energy data files are byte-exact source material.
#
# Several of these formats are fixed-width positional TEXT: UKOOA P1/90 and
# SEG-P1 navigation, LAS well logs, ZMAP+ grids and ECLIPSE GRDECL decks. Git
# would otherwise treat them as text and normalise their line endings, which
# rewrites the bytes of files this repository ships as real, unmodified
# third-party data and whose provenance ATTRIBUTION.md asserts. A P1/90 file
# lost 134 bytes to that normalisation before this file existed.
#
# The binary ones (SEG-Y, SEG-D, DLIS, LIS, shapefiles, GeoTIFF, ECLIPSE
# output, RESQML packages, ROFF and Irap binary) are detected as binary by
# content, but they are listed anyway so the rule is stated rather than
# relied upon. Irap binary matters more than most: the demo asserts that its
# .gri fixture is byte-for-byte what Equinor's xtgeo writes for that surface,
# and content detection is not the place to rest a claim like that.
*.p190  -text
*.p1    -text
*.segp1 -text
*.sgp   -text
*.las   -text
*.zmap  -text
*.grdecl -text
*.irap  -text
*.irapasc -text
*.roffasc -text
*.segy  -text binary
*.sgy   -text binary
*.segd  -text binary
*.dlis  -text binary
*.lis   -text binary
*.epc   -text binary
*.shp   -text binary
*.shx   -text binary
*.dbf   -text binary
*.tif   -text binary
*.tiff  -text binary
*.egrid -text binary
*.init  -text binary
*.unrst -text binary
*.smspec -text binary
*.gri   -text binary
*.roff  -text binary
